The original-rules test checks that exhaustive search finds no goal. The revised-rules test checks the shortest witness path using the added B→C move. The code and tests have not been executed here.

The least fixed point starts with goal states and repeatedly adds a non-goal state only when it has at least one successor and **all** successors are already in the set. The nonempty-successor condition excludes non-goal dead ends. States left outside the fixed point have a possible maximal execution that avoids the goal, through a dead end or a cycle.

